# The prefilled tables as the CPU sees them once loaded (Bochs' debugger at
# the end of pm_start). Every descriptor of the GDT has DPL 0; its pools of
# LDT and kernel stack descriptors, and its two scratch windows, are still
# empty, and no LDT is loaded: the root's space is made after this point
# (roadmap l4.md L3, L5). Of the IDT's gates only 31h, the kernel's calls,
# has DPL 3: 30h, the system call until l4.md L10, has DPL 0. The kernel's
# data segment starts below the image, at KDATA_BASE, above the kernel's
# stacks. Code and data limits change with the code, so they are left out;
# everything else is checked.
emulators: bochs
break: pm_start.ready
debugger: info gdt 0 137
debugger: info idt 0 0x31
debugger: sreg
---
